ltiples it looks expensive against Energy peers: P/E 17.2 vs 13.4 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 81% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of -16.4% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 5.5% (vs the 8% bar).","The 3 covering analysts target $56.00 on average, 103% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 3% falls short of the cost of capital of 8.8%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.47).","It burns cash (FCF margin -34%).","Earnings quality is mixed: cash conversion of 3.16x, but a weak Piotroski score of 3/9.","ROE of 7% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.1x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 19pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 1.2% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.0x net debt to EBITDA ($0 of cash against $329.3M of debt), and interest cover is thin at 2.7x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.66 in the distress zone, which caps the rating at HOLD.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.33)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 26.6% over 3 years, 20.4% over 5 years and 6.0% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 19%).","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 3.3% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Forward indicators: a backlog worth 10% of annual revenue.","Capex runs 3.3x depreciation (70.5% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is -15, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 3.2%, and institutions hold 94%.","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.7% (2.2% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.1% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 259 employees, each generates about $665K of revenue, 0.3x the Energy median, and productivity has risen 7.2% a year.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$226K per employee.","CEO pay is $1.3M (2x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $8K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INSUFFICIENT DATA","conv":null,"head":"Not enough data to value it: missing price or fair value.","pros":[],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":null,"vc":null,"med":{"pe":13.3952,"ev_ebitda":6.86,"pfcf":14.299,"pb":1.6885,"roic":0.0952,"gross_margin":0.2462,"fcf_margin":0.0754,"div_yield":0.0371}},"ticker":"NGS","date":"2026-11-06"}